 "nasrbo3_explanation": "NaSrBO3: pi~_rs_sft=0.49242519 vs empirical rate 18/232=0.0776 across every RS-SFT sample on disk for this target (both the 32-sample resampling_rate draw AND the 200-sample reference pool). The estimator OVERSTATES the true rate by roughly 6.3x -- not the 'tails underestimated' direction regular Claude's hypothesis 2 predicted, the OPPOSITE: this specific cell is a case where the sparse 8-trace average happened to draw at least one trace assigning this recipe very high probability, and that one trace dominates the mean (log of an average of mostly-near-zero and one large value is pulled toward the large value). Not a canonicaliser or surface-form mismatch (checked: the exact predicted set does appear, hit rate ~7.76%, in both sample groups, so the key itself resolves correctly) -- an estimator-variance artifact specific to whichever traces happened to be among this target's up-to-8."
